1AB9D: 'sub_1AB9D' -> 'drawDeathGraphic'
    bitmap blitter: for each set bit in a 16-word-wide bitmap table (word_1EE6C), plots a point via videoDrawPoint in the given color. Called once from `death` -- this is the death-screen graphic (skull), not general-purpose bitmap code (no other caller).
1AC44: 'sub_1AC44' -> 'waitTimerTicks'
    the actual tick-counting primitive behind `wait`: installs a custom INT 1Ch (system timer tick) handler that increments word_1F18E, busy-waits until it reaches the requested tick count, then restores the original INT 1Ch vector. INT 1Ch fires ~18.2 times/second on real PC hardware, so this is where `wait`'s 'amount' argument gets its real-world time meaning.
1BA27: 'sub_1BA27' -> 'drawSelectItemPanel'
    fills and outlines the item-list panel (x 127-199) for the selectItem dialog, then sets _viewRedrawNeeded. Called once.
19FF1: 'sub_19FF1' -> 'initVideoModeCGA'
    INT 10h AL=4 (CGA 320x200 4-color), BIOS palette 1, plus a direct out to port 3D8h (CGA mode-control register) toggling the composite-color/high-res artifact trick. One of 3 hardware-specific initializers setVideoMode dispatches to by _videoMode.
1C455: 'sub_1C455' -> 'initVideoModeEGA'
    INT 10h AL=0Dh (EGA/VGA 320x200 16-color) plus a 17-byte SET ALL PALETTE REGISTERS call (default_palette). _videoMode==1.
1C42E: 'sub_1C42E' -> 'initVideoModeTandy'
    INT 10h AL=9 (Tandy/PCjr 320x200 16-color) plus the same SET ALL PALETTE REGISTERS call as initVideoModeEGA. _videoMode==2.
1B231: 'sub_1B231' -> 'buildScanlineOffsetTable'
    precomputes a 200-entry (unk_1FAFA) row-to-framebuffer-offset table, with 3 different address-math branches matching CGA's interleaved even/odd scanline memory layout vs. the linear layout of the EGA/Tandy 16-color modes -- called once per setVideoMode, before dispatching to whichever initVideoMode* matches _videoMode.
