    the text-mode-aware read underneath _filbuf: looks up the handle slot, calls _dos_read, and for binary streams returns the raw count -- but for text-mode streams, walks the buffer stripping CR (0Dh) and stopping at Ctrl-Z (1Ah, DOS text EOF marker), then calls _lseek to correct the file position for the extra raw bytes consumed by the stripped CRs.
